# Agent Witch guides (required reading)

## Before substantive edits

1. Read [docs/guides/user-guide/00-philosophy-and-vocabulary.md](../../docs/guides/user-guide/00-philosophy-and-vocabulary.md) for product vocabulary (Mac, Task, Run, Playbook).
2. Open the chapter pair listed in [docs/guides/guide-maintenance.map.json](../../docs/guides/guide-maintenance.map.json) for your path prefix.
3. Read [docs/guides/developer-guide/agent-mistakes-catalog.md](../../docs/guides/developer-guide/agent-mistakes-catalog.md) for recurring agent failures.

Query RAG:

```bash
npm run feature-knowledge:query -- "your topic" --feature=docs
```

## When behavior or examples change

Update **both** the user-guide and developer-guide chapter in the **same PR** as code. Refresh worked examples (commands, URLs, screenshots described in prose) so they match production (**www.agentwitch.com**) and local dev (`npm run dev`).

Run:

```bash
npm run feature-knowledge:index
```

Commit `.feature-knowledge/index.json` with the branch.

## Hooks

Cursor **postToolUse** injects chapter reminders when you edit mapped paths. **stop** nags if `src/` / `db/` / `server.ts` changed without any `docs/guides/**` diff—confirm guides still match or update them.

## Do not

- Contradict [UX simplification](../../docs/product/ux-simplification.md) user terms in user-guide chapters.
- Document CHECK24 hosts as default Agent Witch production.
- Split harness / library / marketplace into separate “runtimes” in guide prose.
